<div class="color-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="color-section color-section--border">
    <div class="color-container">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <a href="/tools">Tools</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span aria-current="page">Color Converter</span>
      </nav>

      <span class="section-label">Industry Tool · Free · No Registration Required</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Color Converter for Garments &amp; Textiles</h1>

      <p class="page-intro">Color accuracy in garment production depends on clear communication between designers, buyers, and manufacturers. This free tool converts between all major color formats — HEX, RGB, CMYK, CIE LAB, LCH, HSL, HSV, NCS, Pantone TCX, RAL Classic, Munsell, and XYZ — so your color intent carries correctly from screen to fabric.</p>
      <p class="page-intro">Use the interactive color wheel or enter any color value manually. The Delta E calculator lets you compare two colors for lab dip approval or pre-shipment inspection, with plain-language match quality ratings used across the industry.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MAIN CONVERTER -->
  <section class="color-section color-section--border">
    <div class="color-container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Color Space Converter — All Formats</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Click anywhere on the color wheel, enter a HEX code, or use the RGB sliders below. All 13 color space values update instantly. Click any Copy button to paste directly into your tech pack, design file, or spec sheet.</p>

      <div class="tool-grid">

        <!-- COLOR WHEEL & PREVIEW -->
        <div class="tool-card">
          <h3 class="tool-card-title">Interactive Color Wheel &amp; Shade Palette</h3>
          <div class="color-wheel-container">
            <canvas id="colorWheel" class="color-wheel-canvas" width="350" height="350"></canvas>
            <div class="color-preview-row">
              <div id="colorPreviewLighter2" class="color-preview" style="background-color: #ff0000;" onclick="selectPreviewColor(0)" title="Lighter shade 2"></div>
              <div id="colorPreviewLighter1" class="color-preview" style="background-color: #ff0000;" onclick="selectPreviewColor(1)" title="Lighter shade 1"></div>
